---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AffiliateButton from '../components/AffiliateButton.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Home Espresso Setup: Machine, Grinder & First-Shot Tips"
  description="Build a home espresso setup around your routine. Compare machine and grinder needs, use a first-shot checklist, and plan cleaning before you buy."
  affiliateDisclosure={true}
>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-700 font-semibold mb-2">Home Espresso Setup Guide</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">Your Home Espresso Setup, Step by Step</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Start with the drinks you make and the preparation you want to do. Then choose compatible equipment,
      plan the complete cost, and use the checklist below for your first shots.
    </p>
    <a href="#first-shot" class="inline-block bg-amber-700 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-800">Go to the setup checklist</a>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-4">Manufacturer-source review: October 15, 2026. Research-based guidance; current seller prices, stock and exact retailer model matches still need checking.</p>
  </div>

  <nav aria-label="Espresso setup sections" class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-10 text-sm">
    <a href="#choose" class="border border-gray-300 rounded-full px-3 py-2 hover:border-amber-700">Choose a workflow</a>
    <a href="#budget" class="border border-gray-300 rounded-full px-3 py-2 hover:border-amber-700">Plan your budget</a>
    <a href="#first-shot" class="border border-gray-300 rounded-full px-3 py-2 hover:border-amber-700">Set up &amp; dial in</a>
    <a href="#care" class="border border-gray-300 rounded-full px-3 py-2 hover:border-amber-700">Cleaning &amp; support</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="choose" class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">1. Choose the preparation you want</h2>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-sm">
      <div id="manual" class="border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 rounded-xl p-5">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Ground coffee &amp; a portafilter</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">You prepare the dose, tamp, brew and empty the basket. Compare milk controls and the grinder or pre-ground coffee your basket needs.</p>
        <a href="/posts/gaggia-classic-pro-vs-breville-bambino-plus/" class="font-semibold text-amber-800 hover:underline">Compare Classic &amp; Bambino workflows →</a>
      </div>
      <div id="pod" class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Capsules</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Choose a capsule system and check the recurring coffee cost. Include separate milk equipment if your chosen machine does not supply it.</p>
        <a href="/posts/best-espresso-machine-under-100/" class="font-semibold text-amber-800 hover:underline">Compare ground coffee &amp; Essenza Mini →</a>
      </div>
      <div id="super-auto" class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Bean-to-cup automation</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Check what the exact model automates and what you still clean. Ask about milk-system care, service and replacement supplies.</p>
        <a href="/posts/best-super-automatic-espresso-machine/" class="font-semibold text-amber-800 hover:underline">Explore bean-to-cup buying questions →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="budget" class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">2. Budget for the complete setup</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Compare this total with your own limit: machine + grinder if needed + missing essentials + coffee and cleaning supplies + delivery and tax. Confirm box contents before adding accessories you already receive.</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-gray-200 rounded-xl mb-4">
      <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
        <caption class="sr-only">What to check before adding espresso equipment to your budget</caption>
        <thead class="bg-gray-50 text-gray-900">
          <tr><th scope="col" class="p-3">Item</th><th scope="col" class="p-3">Decide before buying</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 text-gray-700">
          <tr><th scope="row" class="p-3 font-semibold">Machine &amp; basket</th><td class="p-3">Match the model, regional voltage and supplied basket to the coffee you intend to use.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="p-3 font-semibold">Grinder</th><td class="p-3">For whole beans, check adjustment for your brew method. An integrated grinder and a separate grinder create different upgrade choices.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="p-3 font-semibold">Preparation tools</th><td class="p-3">Check the included tamper and its size; choose a scale that fits your tray and recipe. A milk jug is relevant if you steam milk.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="p-3 font-semibold">Upkeep</th><td class="p-3">Price the exact model's cleaning supplies, filters and service options. Keep optional tools separate from essentials.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">A fixed machine-to-grinder spending ratio cannot establish which setup fits your needs. A budget guide is a starting point, not a current checkout offer.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-amber-800">
      <a href="/posts/best-espresso-machine-under-100/" class="hover:underline">Machine shopping with a $100 limit →</a>
      <a href="/posts/best-burr-grinder-under-100/" class="hover:underline">Manual &amp; electric grinders →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Machine workflow and grinder control</h2>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2">Milk workflow</p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Breville Bambino Plus BES500</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-3">Breville documents automatic and manual milk texturing, PID control and a 54 mm portafilter. Decide whether automatic milk is useful in your routine; it does not grind or dose coffee for you.</p>
        <p class="text-sm mb-4"><a href="https://www.breville.com/en-us/product/bes500" class="text-amber-800 underline">Manufacturer specifications</a></p>
        <AffiliateButton productKey="breville-bambino-plus" />
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">Affiliate retailer link. Check the regional model, contents and current offer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wide font-semibold text-amber-700 mb-2">Grind adjustment</p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Baratza Encore ESP</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-3">The Encore ESP manual separates espresso settings 1–20 from filter settings 21–40. These are steps, not a stepless adjustment system. Match the exact ESP model; another Encore variant's scale is not interchangeable.</p>
        <p class="text-sm mb-4"><a href="https://assets.breville.com/ZCG495/manual-encoreesp-v1-0-en-010923.pdf" class="text-amber-800 underline">Manufacturer operating manual</a></p>
        <AffiliateButton productKey="baratza-encore-esp" />
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">Affiliate retailer link. The stored retailer/model match and offer remain unverified.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-4">Considering a Gaggia? Identify its revision first. <a href="https://www.gaggia.com/manual-machines/new-classic-e24/" class="text-amber-800 underline">Gaggia's E24 page</a> specifies a brass boiler and 58 mm filter-holder; those details do not establish the contents of an older Classic Pro listing.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="first-shot" class="mb-10 border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 rounded-xl p-5 sm:p-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">3. Your first-shot setup checklist</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 mb-5">Keep your exact machine and grinder manuals nearby. This checklist helps you organize preparation; their operating and cleaning instructions take priority.</p>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-700">
      <li><strong class="text-gray-900">Prepare the machine and workspace.</strong> Check reservoir access, tray clearance and a stable surface. Complete the manual's first-use rinse or priming sequence before brewing.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-gray-900">Choose the matching basket.</strong> Breville's BES500 manual distinguishes single-wall baskets for freshly ground coffee from dual-wall baskets intended for pre-ground coffee. Do not assume every machine uses the same basket.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-gray-900">Write down a starting recipe.</strong> Use a recipe suited to your basket and coffee. Record the dose, grinder setting, beverage yield and elapsed time instead of relying on an unmarked scoop or cup.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-gray-900">Make one change at a time.</strong> Compare the result with your recipe and taste preference. For the Encore ESP, Baratza advises adjusting within its espresso range; do not copy a setting from a different grinder model.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-gray-900">Finish the routine.</strong> If making milk drinks, follow your machine's steaming sequence. Follow the matching instructions for purging, wiping and cleaning after use. Note what you would repeat or change next time.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mt-5">Sources: <a href="https://www.breville.com/content/dam/breville/us/en/assets/miscellaneous/instruction-manual/espresso/BES500-instruction-manual.pdf" class="underline">BES500 manual</a> and <a href="https://www.baratza.com/en-au/blog/product-guides/dialing-in-espresso" class="underline">Baratza dialing-in guide</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="care" class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">4. Plan cleaning and support before purchase</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">Find the exact model's instructions for the basket, steam wand, water system and descaling. Use its specified supplies and schedule; a generic monthly rule may not match your machine or water.</p>
    <p class="text-gray-700">For a used or older machine, ask about condition, included parts, local service and returns. A community modification or a brand name does not guarantee a ten-year lifespan. Confirm warranty terms for your region and seller.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Common setup questions</h2>
    <div class="divide-y divide-gray-200 border-y border-gray-200 text-sm">
      <details class="py-4">
        <summary class="font-semibold text-gray-900 cursor-pointer">Do I need a separate grinder immediately?</summary>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-3">It depends on the machine, basket and coffee you choose. A capsule workflow has different requirements from whole-bean preparation; some baskets accept pre-ground coffee. Check the matching manual before adding equipment.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="py-4">
        <summary class="font-semibold text-gray-900 cursor-pointer">Will one tamper fit any espresso machine?</summary>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-3">Match the basket's required size and fit. The two examples above use different nominal sizes: 54 mm for the Bambino Plus and 58 mm for the Classic E24.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="py-4">
        <summary class="font-semibold text-gray-900 cursor-pointer">Which setup makes the best espresso?</summary>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-3">We have not physically compared these setups. Choose for the preparation and maintenance you will use, then verify the model, complete price and return terms. A pump-pressure number alone is not a flavor ranking.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Choose your next guide</h2>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
      <a href="/posts/gaggia-classic-pro-vs-breville-bambino-plus/" class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 font-semibold text-amber-800 hover:border-amber-500">Classic or Bambino: compare preparation →</a>
      <a href="/posts/best-burr-grinder-under-100/" class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 font-semibold text-amber-800 hover:border-amber-500">Compare manual and electric grinder controls →</a>
      <a href="/posts/best-espresso-at-home-beginners-guide/" class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 font-semibold text-amber-800 hover:border-amber-500">Explore espresso preparation basics →</a>
      <a href="/methodology/" class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 font-semibold text-amber-800 hover:border-amber-500">How we research equipment →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
